WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:14.514
[♪ majestic orchestral music playing]

2
00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:29.780
[♪ music swells]

3
00:01:15.826 --> 00:01:18.453
[♪ music continues playing]

4
00:02:42.204 --> 00:02:43.538
[♪ music fades]

5
00:02:44.456 --> 00:02:46.708
[Eliza] A long, long time ago,

6
00:02:46.792 --> 00:02:49.419
there existed the Eastern Empire,

7
00:02:49.503 --> 00:02:53.173
a kingdom where magic
was created from the arcane,

8
00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:56.176
a place where
the sun's light reached first.

9
00:02:56.259 --> 00:02:57.594
SOVIESHU'S EAST PALACE

10
00:02:57.678 --> 00:03:02.432
Every corner of the Imperial Palace
was filled with peace and happiness.

11
00:03:02.516 --> 00:03:03.642
EAST PALACE GARDEN
EAST PALACE

12
00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:07.145
Before long,
the cold armor of the battlefield

13
00:03:07.229 --> 00:03:09.439
had become a gentle warmth.

14
00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:11.900
My Emperor, Sovieshu.

15
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:12.984
NAVIER'S WEST PALACE

16
00:03:13.068 --> 00:03:15.070
My Empress, Navier.

17
00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:18.949
The two had become husband and wife
at a young age,

18
00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.576
promising to be each other's light.

19
00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:27.457
For Navier's sake,
Sovieshu had never taken a mistress.

20
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:34.339
But recently, rumors began to spread
that unease was sprouting between them.

21
00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:40.178
This was because there still remained
no child between the pair.

22
00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:43.974
The people, too, began to whisper.

23
00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:48.687
Yet Navier and Sovieshu remained
as steadfast as ever,

24
00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:52.524
their strength could not be shaken
by such words.

25
00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:55.694
[♪ captivating music playing]

26
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:23.764
[♪ music fades]

27
00:04:55.629 --> 00:04:56.963
Where are you going?

28
00:04:57.047 --> 00:04:59.424
To check the speech for New Year's Day.

29
00:05:00.258 --> 00:05:01.760
[Sovieshu sighs softly]

30
00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:03.678
[laughs] Emperor.

31
00:05:09.726 --> 00:05:12.145
How about this for the ceremony?

32
00:05:13.063 --> 00:05:14.689
This would sound good.

33
00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.406
My Empress Navier

34
00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:27.285
is pregnant with her first child.

35
00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:33.166
At long last,
a baby will be born in the palace

36
00:05:34.251 --> 00:05:35.836
to the royal line.

37
00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:40.298
People, rejoice.

38
00:05:41.675 --> 00:05:42.801
A blessing.

39
00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.026
[birds chirping]

40
00:06:01.736 --> 00:06:05.490
[Navier] "The cold armor clung
to our skin so tightly that

41
00:06:05.574 --> 00:06:07.951
"we could not even prize it off,

42
00:06:08.493 --> 00:06:10.662
"and only the hot blood of our enemies

43
00:06:10.745 --> 00:06:13.456
"could melt away the biting cold.

44
00:06:14.332 --> 00:06:18.211
"Our swords and our shields
have not rusted at all."

45
00:06:22.799 --> 00:06:24.634
[bird screeches]

46
00:06:27.178 --> 00:06:28.179
"A blade…

47
00:06:29.014 --> 00:06:30.515
"A blade that shines."

48
00:06:33.977 --> 00:06:35.020
[rustling]

49
00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:38.940
[horse snorts]

50
00:06:39.024 --> 00:06:41.026
[footsteps approaching]

51
00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:50.410
[♪ gentle music playing]

52
00:06:58.585 --> 00:06:59.753
Hmm.

53
00:06:59.836 --> 00:07:01.212
You're having a little one.

54
00:07:07.302 --> 00:07:08.553
[bird screeches]

55
00:07:19.814 --> 00:07:22.192
[tent door rustles]

56
00:07:30.825 --> 00:07:32.160
[Sovieshu exhales softly]

57
00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:36.665
A pardon for my uncle is being discussed.

58
00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.219
The consensus is leaning
against incarcerating a royal

59
00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:50.345
for so long.

60
00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:56.267
He's the man who tried to seize power
right after the death of the late Emperor.

61
00:07:57.519 --> 00:07:58.520
Believe me,

62
00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:01.523
if he's freed, it puts us in jeopardy.

63
00:08:02.607 --> 00:08:03.608
Mmm.

64
00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:05.985
[sighs]

65
00:08:11.866 --> 00:08:13.702
If only we had a child, Empress…

66
00:08:17.455 --> 00:08:20.041
no one would dare challenge for my throne.

67
00:08:34.597 --> 00:08:36.015
[Sovieshu sighs heavily]

68
00:08:45.942 --> 00:08:47.110
Let's go hunting.

69
00:08:49.821 --> 00:08:51.239
Come with me tomorrow.

70
00:09:02.292 --> 00:09:03.293
[Sovieshu sighs]

71
00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:07.338
[Marquess Lante] The hunt begins.

72
00:09:07.422 --> 00:09:09.466
Set up the barrier!

73
00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.182
[♪ enchanting music playing]

74
00:09:27.901 --> 00:09:29.277
[chimes]

75
00:09:33.782 --> 00:09:34.949
How long has it been

76
00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:37.744
since we did something like this?

77
00:09:38.369 --> 00:09:39.496
I couldn't say.

78
00:09:40.663 --> 00:09:41.831
It must be a while.

79
00:09:43.083 --> 00:09:45.168
But I do enjoy just talking with you.

80
00:09:45.251 --> 00:09:48.671
I'll never forget that first day
we went out hunting.

81
00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:52.258
In those days, I was
a more accomplished archer than you were.

82
00:09:53.718 --> 00:09:54.803
I'm grateful now.

83
00:09:57.514 --> 00:09:58.515
For what?

84
00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:01.309
You always made sure
to catch less than I did.

85
00:10:01.392 --> 00:10:02.519
Held back.

86
00:10:03.228 --> 00:10:04.354
You noticed that?

87
00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:08.066
You shan't get a break today.

88
00:10:09.442 --> 00:10:10.610
[chuckles]

89
00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:18.451
[honking]

90
00:10:18.535 --> 00:10:19.744
[bells jingling]

91
00:10:19.828 --> 00:10:21.454
[beaters yelling indistinctly]

92
00:10:24.874 --> 00:10:25.917
[Sovieshu] Hyah!

93
00:10:26.584 --> 00:10:27.877
[horse whinnies]

94
00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.431
[bells jingling faintly]

95
00:10:41.015 --> 00:10:42.058
[horse neighing]

96
00:10:42.142 --> 00:10:43.268
[bells jingling]

97
00:10:43.351 --> 00:10:45.353
[panting]

98
00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:47.105
[guard] Hyah!

99
00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:49.149
Hyah!

100
00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:51.734
[guards panting]

101
00:10:52.819 --> 00:10:53.862
[Sovieshu] Hyah!

102
00:10:53.945 --> 00:10:55.947
[bird cawing]

103
00:10:59.534 --> 00:11:00.952
[bells jingle softly]

104
00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:04.539
[Artina] Wait.

105
00:11:05.999 --> 00:11:07.167
[bells jingling]

106
00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.175
-[jingling]
-[beater yelling]

107
00:11:17.051 --> 00:11:18.595
-[grunts]
-[horse whinnies]

108
00:11:18.678 --> 00:11:20.013
[exclaiming, yelps]

109
00:11:20.096 --> 00:11:22.724
[grunting]

110
00:11:22.807 --> 00:11:24.893
[groaning]

111
00:11:24.976 --> 00:11:26.186
[flies buzzing]

112
00:11:26.269 --> 00:11:27.270
Ugh!

113
00:11:28.271 --> 00:11:29.480
[gasps]

114
00:11:29.564 --> 00:11:31.065
[screaming]

115
00:11:31.149 --> 00:11:32.358
Whoa.

116
00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:33.985
[horse neighing]

117
00:11:34.068 --> 00:11:35.904
[exclaiming in fear]

118
00:11:36.779 --> 00:11:38.281
[panting]

119
00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.449
[flies buzzing]

120
00:11:39.532 --> 00:11:41.409
[♪ ominous music playing]

121
00:11:48.458 --> 00:11:49.459
[horse snorts]

122
00:11:50.335 --> 00:11:51.711
[beater] Oi!

123
00:11:52.754 --> 00:11:54.464
-[bells jingling]
-Oi!

124
00:12:01.804 --> 00:12:02.931
[jingling]

125
00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.232
[♪ foreboding music playing]

126
00:12:13.274 --> 00:12:14.817
[rumbling]

127
00:12:14.901 --> 00:12:15.944
[screams]

128
00:12:17.779 --> 00:12:18.780
[bird cawing]

129
00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.791
[♪ low, tense music playing]

130
00:12:36.381 --> 00:12:37.382
[bow creaks softly]

131
00:12:38.258 --> 00:12:39.300
[snorting]

132
00:12:41.344 --> 00:12:42.512
[clinks]

133
00:12:42.595 --> 00:12:43.596
[rumbling]

134
00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:44.806
[boar squeals]

135
00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:54.524
-[beater] What's the matter, Your Majesty?
-[Navier] Quiet.

136
00:12:54.607 --> 00:12:55.900
Oh.

137
00:13:14.877 --> 00:13:16.212
The bell, now.

138
00:13:18.673 --> 00:13:19.841
[bow creaks]

139
00:13:26.055 --> 00:13:27.307
[jingling]

140
00:13:28.433 --> 00:13:30.393
[low rumbling, thumps]

141
00:13:31.144 --> 00:13:32.145
[jingling]

142
00:13:32.228 --> 00:13:34.230
[loud rumbling]

143
00:13:38.109 --> 00:13:39.110
[trees thud]

144
00:13:39.193 --> 00:13:41.362
[horns blaring]

145
00:13:43.448 --> 00:13:44.449
What's that sound?

146
00:13:44.532 --> 00:13:46.701
It means danger, Your Majesty.
We should flee at once.

147
00:13:46.784 --> 00:13:48.995
-Find the Empress first.
-Of course. Ha!

148
00:13:49.078 --> 00:13:50.079
Hyah!

149
00:13:50.913 --> 00:13:52.498
Hyah! Hyah!

150
00:13:52.582 --> 00:13:54.584
-[bells jingling]
-[beaters panting]

151
00:13:58.171 --> 00:13:59.797
[panting]

152
00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:05.136
[bells jingling]

153
00:14:08.806 --> 00:14:11.184
[panting]

154
00:14:12.977 --> 00:14:13.978
[grunts]

155
00:14:17.607 --> 00:14:18.816
[person screaming]

156
00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:19.942
Whoa.

157
00:14:23.321 --> 00:14:24.405
Hyah!

158
00:14:25.907 --> 00:14:27.825
-Your Majesty.
-Protect the hunting grounds, be careful.

159
00:14:27.909 --> 00:14:29.410
I'll lure it away from here.

160
00:14:31.412 --> 00:14:32.955
-Hup!
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

161
00:14:33.039 --> 00:14:35.041
[bells jingling]

162
00:14:38.836 --> 00:14:40.838
[rumbling]

163
00:14:42.715 --> 00:14:44.258
[breathing heavily]

164
00:14:45.802 --> 00:14:47.303
[bells jingling]

165
00:14:51.224 --> 00:14:52.767
[horse neighs]

166
00:14:58.189 --> 00:14:59.232
[exhales]

167
00:15:00.942 --> 00:15:02.693
[bells jingling]

168
00:15:05.571 --> 00:15:07.323
[screeching]

169
00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.412
[♪ suspenseful music continues playing]

170
00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:21.921
[screeching]

171
00:15:30.429 --> 00:15:32.140
[continues screeching]

172
00:15:54.245 --> 00:15:56.038
[rumbling]

173
00:16:04.672 --> 00:16:06.299
[chimes]

174
00:16:11.971 --> 00:16:13.973
[♪ music fades]

175
00:16:14.056 --> 00:16:15.099
[panting]

176
00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:29.906
[breathing heavily]

177
00:16:29.989 --> 00:16:31.908
[screeching]

178
00:16:47.798 --> 00:16:49.842
[bird screeches in the distance]

179
00:17:06.067 --> 00:17:07.068
[panting]

180
00:17:07.652 --> 00:17:09.570
[yelps, groans]

181
00:17:09.654 --> 00:17:11.364
-[screaming]
-[assassin 1 laughing]

182
00:17:11.447 --> 00:17:12.782
Where are you going now, huh?

183
00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:14.325
[assassins laughing]

184
00:17:14.408 --> 00:17:15.993
We've got you this time.

185
00:17:16.077 --> 00:17:18.287
-[grunts]
-[assassins laughing]

186
00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:21.290
-Whoa.
-[assassin 1] Stay still, damn it.

187
00:17:21.374 --> 00:17:23.584
-[victim grunting]
-[assassin 2] Stay still. Come on.

188
00:17:23.668 --> 00:17:25.795
-[victim groaning, panting]
-Hold still.

189
00:17:25.878 --> 00:17:26.879
-Huh?
-[victim whimpers]

190
00:17:26.963 --> 00:17:28.089
That bastard, who is he?

191
00:17:28.798 --> 00:17:30.716
Did he follow this wench here?

192
00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:33.052
-Sir, don't go!
-[assassin 2] Stay still!

193
00:17:33.135 --> 00:17:35.680
-[victim] Help me, please!
-[assassin 1] This doesn't concern you.

194
00:17:35.763 --> 00:17:37.723
-Please help me!
-[assassin 1] Hey, hey, hey.

195
00:17:37.807 --> 00:17:39.976
[assassin 2]
Where are you running off to? Ah, shit.

196
00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:41.519
[assassin 1] Who are you?

197
00:17:41.602 --> 00:17:43.396
-Your horse looks nice.
-[victim] Sir, please…

198
00:17:43.479 --> 00:17:44.689
-[assassin 1] Huh?
-[victim grunts]

199
00:17:44.772 --> 00:17:46.607
-I want it.
-[assassin 2 grunts]

200
00:17:46.691 --> 00:17:47.817
Get off!

201
00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:49.527
[grunts]

202
00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:50.945
[grunts]

203
00:17:51.028 --> 00:17:52.446
-[sword clangs]
-[grunts]

204
00:17:53.614 --> 00:17:55.157
[yelling]

205
00:17:55.241 --> 00:17:57.535
-[Sovieshu] Hyah!
-[horse whinnies]

206
00:17:57.618 --> 00:17:59.537
[neighing]

207
00:18:01.163 --> 00:18:02.540
[gasps]

208
00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.042
[♪ enchanting music playing]

209
00:18:13.217 --> 00:18:14.510
You little…

210
00:18:16.345 --> 00:18:17.722
[grunting]

211
00:18:17.805 --> 00:18:19.724
[groaning]

212
00:18:20.224 --> 00:18:21.767
[body thuds]

213
00:18:21.851 --> 00:18:23.686
[gasps, groaning]

214
00:18:23.769 --> 00:18:25.980
[screaming]

215
00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.442
[hoofbeats approaching]

216
00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:31.736
Whoa.

217
00:18:31.819 --> 00:18:33.279
Her Majesty is safe, my lord.

218
00:18:40.703 --> 00:18:41.704
The assassin.

219
00:18:41.787 --> 00:18:43.164
I want him caught alive.

220
00:18:43.247 --> 00:18:44.582
-Tell the Empress.
-Yes, Your Majesty.

221
00:18:44.665 --> 00:18:45.666
Ha!

222
00:18:46.167 --> 00:18:47.752
[hoofbeats receding]

223
00:18:50.046 --> 00:18:51.380
[whimpering softly]

224
00:18:51.464 --> 00:18:53.466
[♪ gentle music playing]

225
00:19:29.293 --> 00:19:31.295
[♪ music continues playing]

226
00:19:48.562 --> 00:19:49.647
[horse snorts]

227
00:19:57.238 --> 00:19:58.781
[Sovieshu] Who are you?

228
00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:00.866
[victim] I am…

229
00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.578
Rashta is my name,

230
00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:06.747
noble sir.

231
00:20:08.249 --> 00:20:09.375
"Noble"?

232
00:20:10.334 --> 00:20:11.419
[chuckles softly]

233
00:20:17.007 --> 00:20:19.009
[♪ gentle music continues playing]

234
00:20:34.066 --> 00:20:35.609
[horn blowing]

235
00:20:35.693 --> 00:20:37.236
[Eliza] He must have returned.

236
00:20:41.449 --> 00:20:44.160
Your Majesty,
I heard three murderers ambushed you.

237
00:20:44.243 --> 00:20:46.370
-You're not hurt, are you?
-No, not at all.

238
00:20:46.454 --> 00:20:48.080
I was worried about you.

239
00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.209
Is it them on the cart?

240
00:20:54.628 --> 00:20:56.839
And you? I heard you encountered a beast.

241
00:20:57.423 --> 00:20:58.716
I trust you're not hurt?

242
00:20:59.383 --> 00:21:00.509
No, I'm well.

243
00:21:01.093 --> 00:21:03.554
The knights are searching for any others,
so head indoors now.

244
00:21:04.263 --> 00:21:06.682
As for the assassins, order silence.
Keep all of this quiet.

245
00:21:06.766 --> 00:21:08.434
I will, Your Majesty.

246
00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.616
[♪ captivating music playing]

247
00:21:30.664 --> 00:21:32.666
[♪ music swells]

248
00:21:45.638 --> 00:21:47.890
I heard you were hurt, my lady.

249
00:21:59.026 --> 00:22:01.153
The royal physician is here, Your Majesty.

250
00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.703
[Laura] Oh my goodness!

251
00:22:12.832 --> 00:22:14.041
Oh.

252
00:22:14.124 --> 00:22:15.751
Oh dear! [inhales sharply]

253
00:22:17.253 --> 00:22:18.254
[sighs]

254
00:22:18.712 --> 00:22:22.466
[physician] Fortunately,
the muscle was not torn, Your Majesty.

255
00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:24.218
It could have been much worse.

256
00:22:33.018 --> 00:22:34.770
Has His Highness not returned?

257
00:22:34.854 --> 00:22:38.315
I'll be told straight away
as soon as he gets back to the palace.

258
00:22:38.399 --> 00:22:39.400
Your Majesty, he'll be fine.

259
00:22:39.483 --> 00:22:41.527
Searching for an assassin
must take a while.

260
00:22:43.153 --> 00:22:44.154
-[gasps]
-Assassin?

261
00:22:50.411 --> 00:22:51.620
[door opens]

262
00:22:51.704 --> 00:22:53.956
[footsteps receding]

263
00:22:54.039 --> 00:22:55.082
[door closes]

264
00:22:55.875 --> 00:22:57.501
His Highness has ordered

265
00:22:57.585 --> 00:23:00.379
that no one speak of what happened
this afternoon.

266
00:23:00.462 --> 00:23:02.047
Take care not to forget.

267
00:23:02.131 --> 00:23:03.465
[both] Yes, Your Majesty.

268
00:23:04.008 --> 00:23:06.677
-Countess, make sure this is done.
-I will, my lady.

269
00:23:07.553 --> 00:23:08.846
Has everybody gathered?

270
00:23:08.929 --> 00:23:11.265
Yes, but it includes Lady Albani.

271
00:23:14.476 --> 00:23:15.686
Albani is here?

272
00:23:17.354 --> 00:23:20.566
Apparently, she intends
to petition in earnest

273
00:23:20.649 --> 00:23:21.984
and plead for her husband's release.

274
00:23:25.154 --> 00:23:26.363
Treat her with care.

275
00:23:26.989 --> 00:23:28.574
She is a member of this house.

276
00:23:28.657 --> 00:23:29.658
[Eliza] Understood.

277
00:23:29.742 --> 00:23:31.076
[noble 1] Oh, yes!

278
00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:33.078
[Verdi] Her Majesty the Empress.

279
00:23:34.121 --> 00:23:35.956
[nobles] Your Majesty.

280
00:23:37.625 --> 00:23:38.918
I trust you're all well?

281
00:23:39.001 --> 00:23:40.753
We heard that you went out on a hunt.

282
00:23:40.836 --> 00:23:42.755
It was marvelous to go riding.
I've missed it.

283
00:23:42.838 --> 00:23:44.965
[gasps] Oh my! Did you get hurt?

284
00:23:45.549 --> 00:23:46.717
I brushed against a tree.

285
00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:50.054
[gasps] Really, Your Majesty,
you're astonishing.

286
00:23:50.137 --> 00:23:51.513
Hunting, of all things!

287
00:23:51.597 --> 00:23:54.391
[Navier] I heard from Lord Kosair
that your son played a great role

288
00:23:54.475 --> 00:23:55.851
in defeating the Springwater Bandits.

289
00:23:55.935 --> 00:23:58.771
Do you mean
that Lord Kosair knows of my son?

290
00:23:58.854 --> 00:24:00.147
-Of course.
-[Pidot gasps]

291
00:24:00.230 --> 00:24:02.524
My brother awarded
your late son with a medal.

292
00:24:02.608 --> 00:24:03.984
-Oh!
-Oh my.

293
00:24:04.068 --> 00:24:05.611
-Oh, good heavens!
-Oh my goodness!

294
00:24:07.947 --> 00:24:09.031
[clears throat]

295
00:24:13.744 --> 00:24:16.163
Albani, my dear, it's been a while.

296
00:24:17.706 --> 00:24:19.667
It's a real pleasure to be here.

297
00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:21.585
I'm delighted, Your Majesty.

298
00:24:27.508 --> 00:24:29.343
You're always welcome in this court.

299
00:24:29.885 --> 00:24:31.220
Thank you.

300
00:24:31.303 --> 00:24:33.138
I so enjoy visiting you.

301
00:24:33.222 --> 00:24:36.016
Please do let me share
in your worries, my lady.

302
00:24:37.184 --> 00:24:38.978
Wouldn't it be better
to have no worries at all?

303
00:24:39.937 --> 00:24:43.399
Nevertheless, your devotion
is much appreciated.

304
00:24:44.108 --> 00:24:46.402
-Hmm.
-[nobles chuckling]

305
00:24:51.323 --> 00:24:52.324
[scoffs]

306
00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:54.493
[scoffs]

307
00:25:00.833 --> 00:25:03.502
[noble 2] This may be
a rather vulgar topic, but…

308
00:25:04.086 --> 00:25:07.506
I hear Count Yuji was caught
having another affair.

309
00:25:07.589 --> 00:25:09.425
[noble 3] Who's the woman this time?

310
00:25:09.508 --> 00:25:11.760
[noble 2] I heard
it's some young commoner.

311
00:25:11.844 --> 00:25:14.346
Still, how fortunate
that this one's not a slave.

312
00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:16.140
[nobles laugh]

313
00:25:16.849 --> 00:25:18.767
You know, he really never
gives it a rest, does he?

314
00:25:18.851 --> 00:25:19.852
[nobles laugh]

315
00:25:22.980 --> 00:25:24.106
[cart stops]

316
00:25:24.189 --> 00:25:25.399
[horse snorts]

317
00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:32.281
[guard] Get down.

318
00:25:35.117 --> 00:25:36.201
[Eliza] Your Majesty.

319
00:25:38.203 --> 00:25:41.623
His Majesty the Emperor has arrived safely
at the palace, my lady.

320
00:25:46.670 --> 00:25:48.672
[♪ majestic music playing]

321
00:26:02.686 --> 00:26:04.063
[rat squeaking]

322
00:26:06.565 --> 00:26:07.733
[Rashta panting]

323
00:26:07.816 --> 00:26:08.817
[guard] Follow me.

324
00:26:11.278 --> 00:26:12.905
[assassin] Don't hurt me! [grunts]

325
00:26:12.988 --> 00:26:14.907
I don't wanna die! [groans]

326
00:26:16.075 --> 00:26:18.243
You dared to point your weapon
at the Royal Emperor.

327
00:26:18.827 --> 00:26:20.412
I didn't know it was him…

328
00:26:20.496 --> 00:26:21.705
[grunts]

329
00:26:22.206 --> 00:26:23.540
You better start talking.

330
00:26:23.624 --> 00:26:25.042
[assassin] I'll do whatever you order.

331
00:26:25.125 --> 00:26:26.335
Please! Just spare my life!

332
00:26:26.418 --> 00:26:27.669
-[chain clinks]
-[choking]

333
00:26:27.753 --> 00:26:29.463
-[squeaking]
-[commander] Who is behind this?

334
00:26:29.546 --> 00:26:31.465
-Who ordered you to do it?
-[assassin groaning]

335
00:26:31.548 --> 00:26:33.175
Speak if you want to live!

336
00:26:33.258 --> 00:26:35.260
[Rashta breathing shakily]

337
00:26:40.641 --> 00:26:42.434
-[keys jingling]
-[cell door opening]

338
00:26:42.518 --> 00:26:43.519
[whimpering]

339
00:26:48.232 --> 00:26:49.608
[Rashta] Please, spare me.

340
00:26:49.691 --> 00:26:51.527
Please spare me. Please spare me.

341
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:54.947
Please, I beg you, spare me. [sobbing]

342
00:26:57.950 --> 00:26:58.951
Please spare me.

343
00:26:59.034 --> 00:27:00.828
[sobbing] Where are you taking me?

344
00:27:09.878 --> 00:27:11.338
[crying]

345
00:27:17.594 --> 00:27:18.595
[door closes]

346
00:27:19.096 --> 00:27:20.597
[grunting softly]

347
00:27:30.232 --> 00:27:31.525
[breathing shakily]

348
00:27:31.608 --> 00:27:32.609
[zipper unzips]

349
00:27:35.153 --> 00:27:37.155
[♪ soft music playing]

350
00:27:43.036 --> 00:27:44.538
[exclaims]

351
00:27:59.887 --> 00:28:00.971
WHEN SUCH A CALM DAY WAS GRANTED TO ME,

352
00:28:01.054 --> 00:28:02.639
THE FIRST THING THAT CAME TO MIND
WAS… A CHILD.

353
00:28:02.723 --> 00:28:04.725
[♪ somber music playing]

354
00:28:07.769 --> 00:28:09.646
[Sovieshu]
If only we had a child, Empress…

355
00:28:11.273 --> 00:28:13.859
no one would dare challenge for my throne.

356
00:28:27.581 --> 00:28:29.041
[Eliza] You should go to bed.

357
00:28:29.124 --> 00:28:30.751
It's getting very late, my lady.

358
00:28:35.672 --> 00:28:37.466
Is there any more news about the assassin?

359
00:28:37.549 --> 00:28:39.885
And has his name been discovered?

360
00:28:39.968 --> 00:28:41.136
Or who ordered it?

361
00:28:43.347 --> 00:28:45.349
I've heard nothing. Shall I go and ask?

362
00:28:46.808 --> 00:28:47.809
No, don't go.

363
00:28:48.477 --> 00:28:49.645
We'll hear more in the morning.

364
00:28:52.022 --> 00:28:53.023
Sleep well then.

365
00:29:00.822 --> 00:29:01.907
[door opens]

366
00:29:02.824 --> 00:29:03.825
[door closes]

367
00:29:04.451 --> 00:29:05.994
[hooves clopping]

368
00:29:11.166 --> 00:29:12.584
[horse neighs softly]

369
00:29:12.668 --> 00:29:13.752
[sighs]

370
00:29:15.545 --> 00:29:16.546
[Charles] How did it go?

371
00:29:16.630 --> 00:29:17.756
[Albani] The ghastly witch.

372
00:29:17.839 --> 00:29:19.925
Already, all of high society
has been filled

373
00:29:20.008 --> 00:29:21.510
with people on the Empress' side.

374
00:29:21.593 --> 00:29:24.388
The sly girl.
We should've killed her off 15 years ago.

375
00:29:24.471 --> 00:29:26.181
It was that cunning wench's little schemes

376
00:29:26.264 --> 00:29:28.642
that let that Sovieshu boy
steal the palace!

377
00:29:28.725 --> 00:29:31.687
[groans] And in my veins, the blood
still boils when I think of that day!

378
00:29:31.770 --> 00:29:33.522
[laughs wryly] Good heavens.

379
00:29:33.605 --> 00:29:36.692
Everyone there praises and flatters
and fawns all over her.

380
00:29:36.775 --> 00:29:38.902
And she loves it, that bogus empress.

381
00:29:38.986 --> 00:29:40.737
I'll wipe that smile off her face.

382
00:29:40.821 --> 00:29:42.531
-[grunts in frustration]
-[sighs]

383
00:29:43.865 --> 00:29:46.159
Mother, you should be the one
receiving praise.

384
00:29:46.243 --> 00:29:48.245
You and Father should rightfully
have the palace,

385
00:29:48.328 --> 00:29:49.746
not those good-for-nothings.

386
00:29:49.830 --> 00:29:50.831
[groans]

387
00:29:55.460 --> 00:29:56.461
[sighs deeply]

388
00:29:59.172 --> 00:30:00.882
We'll do whatever it takes.

389
00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:05.095
Firstly, we must restore our titles

390
00:30:05.178 --> 00:30:06.388
and get our estate returned.

391
00:30:07.973 --> 00:30:09.224
Understand?

392
00:30:13.311 --> 00:30:14.646
That's our plan…

393
00:30:14.730 --> 00:30:15.814
Mmm?

394
00:30:26.658 --> 00:30:28.660
[♪ mischievous music playing]

395
00:30:38.837 --> 00:30:40.922
[♪ dramatic music playing]

396
00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:45.802
[panting]

397
00:30:48.722 --> 00:30:50.015
[letters thudding]

398
00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:53.226
NEW YEAR'S CEREMONY GUEST LIST

399
00:31:00.609 --> 00:31:05.614
INVITATION TO THE EASTERN EMPIRE'S
NEW YEAR'S CEREMONY

400
00:31:07.991 --> 00:31:09.743
[Laura exhales] My goodness.

401
00:31:16.458 --> 00:31:17.584
[sighs heavily]

402
00:31:21.171 --> 00:31:23.381
-Your Majesty.
-What is it, Laura?

403
00:31:23.465 --> 00:31:24.716
Well…

404
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:25.926
So, His Majesty,

405
00:31:26.802 --> 00:31:29.054
after the hunt, he brought a woman here.

406
00:31:29.137 --> 00:31:30.305
A woman?

407
00:31:30.388 --> 00:31:31.473
Uh-huh.

408
00:31:32.641 --> 00:31:34.518
It sounds like the assassin, does it not?

409
00:31:35.143 --> 00:31:37.145
Oh, no. Not the assassin.

410
00:31:37.229 --> 00:31:40.732
His Majesty rescued a woman
after finding her caught in a beast trap.

411
00:31:49.032 --> 00:31:51.159
[Verdi] So, what about this woman?

412
00:31:51.243 --> 00:31:52.994
[panting] This is what I've heard.

413
00:31:53.078 --> 00:31:55.664
That His Majesty made a real fuss of her.

414
00:31:55.747 --> 00:31:59.376
He ordered a luxurious bath for her
with maids in attendance.

415
00:31:59.459 --> 00:32:02.462
They say that once they took off
her muddy clothes and washed her,

416
00:32:02.546 --> 00:32:04.506
she was completely transformed and…

417
00:32:04.589 --> 00:32:06.550
[inhales deeply] …supremely beautiful.

418
00:32:06.633 --> 00:32:09.803
Now everyone's talking about it,
from the attendants to the maids.

419
00:32:09.886 --> 00:32:11.054
Lady Laura.

420
00:32:12.347 --> 00:32:13.598
Uh…

421
00:32:15.183 --> 00:32:16.560
Please continue speaking.

422
00:32:18.937 --> 00:32:21.481
[Laura] After they cleaned her up,
dressed her in fresh clothes,

423
00:32:21.565 --> 00:32:23.275
and brought her before His Majesty…

424
00:32:23.358 --> 00:32:24.943
Well, His Majesty…

425
00:32:28.029 --> 00:32:29.531
[clinking]

426
00:32:33.160 --> 00:32:34.411
[door opens]

427
00:32:45.380 --> 00:32:46.381
[door closes]

428
00:32:52.095 --> 00:32:54.097
[♪ gentle music playing]

429
00:33:37.182 --> 00:33:38.433
Tell me your name again.

430
00:33:43.688 --> 00:33:45.857
Rashta, Your Majesty.

431
00:33:48.360 --> 00:33:49.527
I deserve…

432
00:33:49.611 --> 00:33:52.280
death for failing
to recognize Your Majesty,

433
00:33:52.864 --> 00:33:54.407
and yet I have only received

434
00:33:54.491 --> 00:33:58.161
such kindness that I can never repay.

435
00:33:58.787 --> 00:34:00.622
I don't know what to do with myself.

436
00:34:17.847 --> 00:34:19.391
[Sovieshu exhales]

437
00:34:30.568 --> 00:34:32.529
Call the physician and get her treated.

438
00:34:38.785 --> 00:34:39.995
[exhales]

439
00:34:53.842 --> 00:34:55.260
Our physician?

440
00:34:56.428 --> 00:34:59.472
He called the imperial physician
for a lowly wench who no one even knows?

441
00:34:59.556 --> 00:35:00.557
Yes!

442
00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:03.518
The Emperor's acting like this girl
has him utterly enchanted.

443
00:35:03.602 --> 00:35:04.978
Lady Laura!

444
00:35:05.061 --> 00:35:07.480
Keep quiet and don't be… insolent.

445
00:35:07.564 --> 00:35:08.898
Oh, no, my lady.

446
00:35:08.982 --> 00:35:11.484
It's dangerous. We need to stamp this out.

447
00:35:11.568 --> 00:35:13.945
Has His Majesty
ever shown interest in any woman

448
00:35:14.029 --> 00:35:15.655
other than Her Majesty the Empress?

449
00:35:15.739 --> 00:35:17.032
He's always said
he'd never take a mistress.

450
00:35:17.115 --> 00:35:18.283
I'd like you to leave.

451
00:35:18.366 --> 00:35:19.868
-No, I just--
-[shushes]

452
00:35:22.203 --> 00:35:24.080
Yes… My lady.

453
00:35:33.298 --> 00:35:35.008
I must ask, why did he take her?

454
00:35:35.925 --> 00:35:37.218
Huh?

455
00:35:37.302 --> 00:35:39.763
After she was washed,
did she go to his chambers?

456
00:35:40.347 --> 00:35:41.431
[gasps softly]

457
00:35:43.558 --> 00:35:45.477
-Did they do it?
-[gasps]

458
00:35:46.061 --> 00:35:47.395
[Eliza] I don't believe for a moment

459
00:35:47.479 --> 00:35:49.898
that His Majesty
would ever behave improperly,

460
00:35:49.981 --> 00:35:52.901
but the ladies-in-waiting
do have a point, Your Majesty.

461
00:35:52.984 --> 00:35:56.780
Perhaps you should speak with him
and ask him what he intends to do.

462
00:35:56.863 --> 00:35:58.865
And mention these assassins as well

463
00:35:58.948 --> 00:36:00.909
to find out what really happened.

464
00:36:03.161 --> 00:36:04.162
I will do.

465
00:36:06.623 --> 00:36:08.667
I need to check the fees
for New Year's Day,

466
00:36:09.292 --> 00:36:10.627
so please send the Minister in.

467
00:36:10.710 --> 00:36:11.753
Yes.

468
00:36:17.717 --> 00:36:19.177
[footsteps receding]

469
00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:20.261
[door opens]

470
00:36:21.596 --> 00:36:23.598
-[door closes]
-[inhales deeply]

471
00:36:36.236 --> 00:36:37.696
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

472
00:36:38.279 --> 00:36:39.364
[chuckles softly]

473
00:36:39.447 --> 00:36:41.241
Go to the Eastern Palace right now.

474
00:36:41.324 --> 00:36:42.742
Find out what's going on.

475
00:36:42.826 --> 00:36:44.577
Something's changed
since His Highness returned

476
00:36:44.661 --> 00:36:45.870
from the royal hunting grounds.

477
00:36:45.954 --> 00:36:47.997
Ask for any news of this girl.

478
00:36:48.707 --> 00:36:50.291
Find out every small detail.

479
00:36:57.966 --> 00:36:59.134
[coughing]

480
00:37:00.552 --> 00:37:02.470
Forgive me, I beg you.

481
00:37:02.554 --> 00:37:04.806
[sobbing] Please spare me.
Have mercy on me.

482
00:37:10.895 --> 00:37:11.896
[sniffs]

483
00:37:11.980 --> 00:37:13.273
[guard] This is good.

484
00:37:18.987 --> 00:37:20.280
He's a manhunter?

485
00:37:20.363 --> 00:37:21.823
Yes, that is what they call

486
00:37:21.906 --> 00:37:24.284
those who hunt down
runaway slaves or criminals.

487
00:37:24.367 --> 00:37:27.203
They strayed into the hunting grounds
while chasing the woman near there.

488
00:37:27.287 --> 00:37:28.580
Can you be certain of that?

489
00:37:28.663 --> 00:37:31.166
We're still questioning him now,
although his story sounds credible.

490
00:37:31.249 --> 00:37:34.377
There's a slave trader who lives
in an estate just near our border.

491
00:37:34.461 --> 00:37:35.670
According to the assailant,

492
00:37:35.754 --> 00:37:38.256
there is quite a large bounty
on the woman's head.

493
00:37:39.841 --> 00:37:41.968
How shall we deal with him,
when we're done?

494
00:37:42.051 --> 00:37:44.012
I'll see to it
once the interrogation's over.

495
00:37:44.095 --> 00:37:45.930
-We'll decide what to do then.
-Yes.

496
00:37:46.014 --> 00:37:48.057
But… Sire… Sire.

497
00:37:50.059 --> 00:37:53.897
You will be careful during your dinner
with the Empress, Your Majesty?

498
00:37:54.439 --> 00:37:55.940
[sucks teeth]

499
00:37:56.024 --> 00:37:57.817
-I'll be there.
-Ah, but…

500
00:37:57.901 --> 00:37:59.903
[screeching]

501
00:37:59.986 --> 00:38:01.988
[♪ majestic music playing]

502
00:38:10.789 --> 00:38:11.790
[screeches]

503
00:38:28.014 --> 00:38:29.682
[screeching]

504
00:38:33.353 --> 00:38:34.354
Where's Her Majesty?

505
00:38:34.437 --> 00:38:36.314
She wanted to take a short walk.
She'll come back.

506
00:38:36.397 --> 00:38:37.899
Did she go on her own?

507
00:38:37.982 --> 00:38:39.567
Well, I'm certain
she has a lot on her mind.

508
00:38:39.651 --> 00:38:42.153
She must be thinking
about this dinner with His Majesty.

509
00:38:44.948 --> 00:38:46.324
Should we let her go?

510
00:38:57.377 --> 00:38:58.586
[exhales softly]

511
00:39:04.676 --> 00:39:05.844
[bird screeches]

512
00:39:06.761 --> 00:39:08.763
[♪ delicate music playing]

513
00:39:24.988 --> 00:39:26.531
I think I know you.

514
00:39:26.614 --> 00:39:27.991
You are just like that bird

515
00:39:29.158 --> 00:39:30.535
who saved me at the hunt.

516
00:39:31.744 --> 00:39:32.745
[chirps]

517
00:39:34.205 --> 00:39:35.373
May I please touch you?

518
00:39:39.711 --> 00:39:40.712
[coos]

519
00:39:42.589 --> 00:39:44.591
[♪ music swells]

520
00:39:46.301 --> 00:39:47.719
[chirps]

521
00:39:54.475 --> 00:39:55.518
[chirping]

522
00:40:00.064 --> 00:40:01.566
You're a pretty little thing.

523
00:40:03.860 --> 00:40:05.028
[chirps]

524
00:40:06.905 --> 00:40:08.281
My goodness, you're a messenger.

525
00:40:09.490 --> 00:40:11.492
I wonder if you're delivering a letter.

526
00:40:28.635 --> 00:40:30.720
[sender] Wouldn't you say
our meeting was fate?

527
00:40:32.597 --> 00:40:33.806
"Was fate"?

528
00:40:37.936 --> 00:40:38.937
[chirping]

529
00:40:40.063 --> 00:40:41.064
Hmm.

530
00:40:52.408 --> 00:40:53.409
[Rashta] Your Majesty.

531
00:41:03.127 --> 00:41:04.295
How's your leg?

532
00:41:05.755 --> 00:41:08.967
It's really doing very well now.
Thanks to you, Your Majesty.

533
00:41:24.649 --> 00:41:26.192
How did you end up like this?

534
00:41:27.026 --> 00:41:30.279
Did your master punish you for wickedness?

535
00:41:33.866 --> 00:41:34.867
[chuckles softly]

536
00:41:36.869 --> 00:41:38.454
I'm not concerned with that.

537
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:43.793
I wish to know all that there is.

538
00:41:45.211 --> 00:41:48.381
Such as who you are
and where you are from.

539
00:41:54.303 --> 00:41:56.305
WOULDN'T YOU SAY OUR MEETING WAS FATE?

540
00:42:02.270 --> 00:42:05.481
[Navier] A fate
that had lost its way found me,

541
00:42:05.565 --> 00:42:07.233
and now I send it back.

542
00:42:10.528 --> 00:42:11.612
May you reach

543
00:42:12.280 --> 00:42:14.407
the fate you seek.

544
00:42:19.662 --> 00:42:20.663
[bird chirps]

545
00:42:29.172 --> 00:42:30.298
Trust me, Rashta.

546
00:42:33.718 --> 00:42:34.719
Emperor…

547
00:42:35.595 --> 00:42:37.847
you should know I didn't do anything bad.

548
00:42:38.765 --> 00:42:41.225
I ran away out of fear of being killed.

549
00:42:41.893 --> 00:42:43.978
I was absolutely petrified.

550
00:42:44.062 --> 00:42:46.189
I was getting beaten badly.

551
00:42:46.272 --> 00:42:47.690
And that's my background.

552
00:42:49.942 --> 00:42:50.943
Hmm, yeah.

553
00:42:51.694 --> 00:42:52.695
It's all right.

554
00:42:53.362 --> 00:42:54.739
I understand very well.

555
00:42:56.282 --> 00:42:58.409
Once this injured leg is better,

556
00:42:59.077 --> 00:43:01.496
I'll be alone
and thrown out of the palace.

557
00:43:02.872 --> 00:43:04.207
No such thing was said.

558
00:43:04.290 --> 00:43:05.541
It's natural.

559
00:43:06.709 --> 00:43:10.838
This palace is not the kind of place
for a lost girl like me.

560
00:43:14.300 --> 00:43:16.302
But I beg you, Your Majesty.

561
00:43:16.385 --> 00:43:19.305
Please do not send me back
to the place where my master is.

562
00:43:19.388 --> 00:43:22.016
If I go, he won't stop beating me
until I'm dead.

563
00:43:22.100 --> 00:43:24.102
[sobbing]

564
00:43:27.563 --> 00:43:28.564
[sighs]

565
00:43:28.648 --> 00:43:30.650
[♪ soft music playing]

566
00:43:56.717 --> 00:43:58.177
Stop your crying.

567
00:44:23.369 --> 00:44:25.371
[♪ music swells]

568
00:44:43.764 --> 00:44:45.141
I will ensure

569
00:44:47.351 --> 00:44:49.604
you never endure such pain again.

570
00:44:55.735 --> 00:44:57.028
[sniffles]

571
00:45:07.413 --> 00:45:09.415
[♪ rousing music playing]

572
00:45:15.087 --> 00:45:16.339
[bird screeches]

573
00:45:33.564 --> 00:45:39.237
THE REMARRIED EMPRESS

574
00:45:40.238 --> 00:45:42.240
[♪ closing theme music playing]

